sequenceDiagram
    title Execution flow — Compilation cadence (precise Rust facade signatures)

    participant Initiator as Initiator (cli / repl)<br/>::main, ::repl
    participant Watcher as Watcher<br/>::watch (OS callback thread)
    participant Sess as Session (CompilerSession)<br/>initiator-thread-only<br/>(watcher channel, REPL cursor, worker pool, warnings)
    participant Shared as Sess.shared (Arc[SharedState])<br/>worker-shareable subset<br/>(symbol_tables, scheduler, cache, kept_dlls, introspection)<br/>per Decision 38 — workers hold Arc clones
    participant Sched as Scheduler<br/>::scheduler::CompileScheduler<br/>(work dispatch + per-symbol/per-module readiness)
    participant Cache as Object cache<br/>::cache::ObjectCache
    participant GotObs as GotObserver<br/>cranelisp_backend::register_got_observer<br/>(extension point — consumer state in src::got_trace)

    Note over Initiator, GotObs: † marks proposed/target API not yet in current code.<br/>Workers, facades, and STs introduced lazily at first use.<br/>All call signatures are the as-designed facade — translate directly to Rust source.<br/>Receiver (&self / &mut self) is implicit in the lifeline.<br/>SharedState is the Arc[T] every worker holds — initiator-side calls touch Sess, worker-side calls touch Shared.<br/>GotObserver registration (extension point per cranelisp_backend::got_observer rustdoc + bounded-contexts.md §3) happens once at session init from int when REPL/trace mode or CRANELISP_GOT_TRACE=1 is active. Production batch: no observer registered, one relaxed null-check load per emit site.

    rect rgb(245, 230, 255)
        Note over Initiator, Sched: ENTRY — register_module runs Phase 0 SYNCHRONOUSLY (parse + structural decls), then dispatches<br/>Phase 0 is the only [&mut SymbolTable] hold (microseconds — entry write lock on the outer DashMap).<br/>After Phase 0 the SymbolTable is reachable only via shared .get() — workers run with [&SymbolTable] + per-entry inner locks.

        alt fresh registration
            Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::register_module(module: &ModuleFullPath, source: Arc[str]) -> Result[(), CranelispError]

            Note over Sess, Shared: PHASE 0 — synchronous setup before scheduler dispatch
            create participant Frontend as Frontend facade<br/>cranelisp_frontend
            Sess ->> Frontend: cranelisp_frontend::parse(source: &str) -> Result[Vec[Sexp], CranelispError]
            Frontend -->> Sess: Ok(Vec[Sexp])
            Sess ->> Frontend: cranelisp_frontend::extract_module_declarations(containing_module: &ModuleFullPath, forms: Vec[Sexp]) -> Result[(StructuralDecls, Vec[Sexp]), CranelispError]
            Frontend -->> Sess: Ok((StructuralDecls { imports, exports, platforms, submodules }, residual_forms: Vec[Sexp]))
            Sess ->> Shared: Sess.shared.symbol_tables.entry(module.clone()).or_default()
            Shared -->> Sess: RefMut[SymbolTable] (brief exclusive — entry write lock)
            create participant ST_m1 as ST[m1]<br/>SymbolTable [generic C=Code, L=()]
            Sess ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::write_structural_decls(decls: StructuralDecls)<br/>(populates imports / exports / platforms / submodules per Decision 33 — file-modules only)
            Note over Sess, Shared: RefMut DROPS — Phase 0 over.<br/>Workers will reach ST[m1] via shared Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(m1) — no more [&mut SymbolTable].

            Sess ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::register_module(module: ModuleFullPath)<br/>(now safe to dispatch PriorityWork::Typecheck — the SymbolTable exists and structural decls are written)
            Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(())
        else watcher re-registration (file changed for already-registered m1)
            Watcher -->> Sess: notify::Event { kind: Modify, paths: [m1.cl] } (channel send, OS thread to Sess channel)
            Note over Sess: watcher events suppressed during REPL eval+print —<br/>processed only while REPL is at prompt waiting for input<br/>(file changes during eval do not invalidate the in-flight evaluation)
            Sess ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::re_register_module(module: &ModuleFullPath) -> bool
            Note over Sched: clears m1 scheduler state,<br/>re-inserts at TypecheckFirst.<br/>(re-registration re-runs Phase 0 — parse the new source + write_structural_decls.)
        end
    end

    Note over Initiator, Sched: Cli pre-exit affordances — block until ALL pending work of that kind completes:<br/>CompilerSession::wait_for_inmem_codegen — until all in-mem code is loaded<br/>CompilerSession::wait_for_object_codegen — until all .o + sidecars are on disk<br/>(REPL doesn't use these — it does its own per-eval coordination)

    Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::wait_for_inmem_codegen() -> Result<(), CranelispError> †
    Sess ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_inmem_complete() -> Result<(), SchedulerError>
    Note over Initiator, Sched: blocked until in-mem complete signal fires (returns later — see below)

    Note over Sched: Scheduler invariants —<br/>at most ONE worker per module during typecheck (ORDERING per Decision 30 — no longer required for lock safety).<br/>Per-symbol mutability via inner DashMap per-key locks (Decisions 25, 33, 38).<br/>Wait/release is per-symbol or per-module readiness.

    rect rgb(220, 235, 255)
        Note over Sched: TYPECHECK PHASE
        Note over Sched: Workers operate on &SymbolTable via Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get. Cache hit via sidecar skips the cluster loop entirely.
        Note over Sched: Per Decision 44 the typecheck surface is a single free function check_forms. The orchestrator process_cluster in the int crate drives it across one cluster.
        Note over Sched: A cluster is one form for non-begin REPL input, or contents of a begin-block for explicit REPL clusters, or the file non-structural forms for batch one-big-cluster.
        Note over Sched: check_forms takes Vec of ParsedEntry plus mutable SymbolTableAccess plus SymbolTables and returns Result of CheckError. It runs over the FULLY-EXPANDED non-macro forms (macro expansion already happened in Pass 1, outside check_forms). Internally it registers non-macro signatures then checks non-macro bodies — these are Passes 2 and 3 of the three-pass module model. Working state lives inside check_forms frame and never crosses the facade.
        Note over Sched: typecheck reads via ctx.current_symbol_table which returns a View union of staging and live in Cluster mode, and writes via ctx.current_symbol_table_mut which returns mutable staging. The 91 register-call sites in program.rs do not change individually.
        Note over Sched: orchestrator owns a transient staging SymbolTable for the cluster, held under mutable borrow inside SymbolTableAccess::Cluster, and commits via insert_cluster atomically into the live SymbolTable on success.
        Note over Sched: On Err of TypeError staging dissolves with the function frame. Live table is byte-identical to pre-cluster state. On Err of Gap the orchestrator drops staging and retries the whole check_forms call against a fresh staging frame.

        create participant PW as Priority Worker<br/>::worker::priority_worker_loop(Arc[SharedState])
        Sched -->> PW: Some(PriorityWork::Typecheck(m1: ModuleFullPath))<br/>(returned from take_priority_work_blocking() the worker was parked in)

        PW ->> Cache: ObjectCache::lookup_sidecar(module: &ModuleFullPath, source_hash: u64) -> CacheLookupResult

        alt cache hit (.meta.json present, schema_version + source_hash match)
            Cache -->> PW: CacheLookupResult::Hit(SymbolTable [generic C=Code, L=()]) — deserialised
            Note over PW, Shared: install entries from cached sidecar — overwrite Sess.shared.symbol_tables[m1] with deserialised value<br/>(this is the one cache-hit case where Phase 0's seed value is replaced wholesale, brief entry write lock)
            PW ->> Shared: Sess.shared.symbol_tables.insert(m1, deserialised_st)
            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_typecheck_done_from_cache(module: &ModuleFullPath)
            Note over Sched: dedicated cache-hit notification —<br/>Sched releases all m1/* typecheck waiters and enqueues PriorityWork::LoadObject(m1)<br/>(.o assumed paired with sidecar — no per-symbol Jit items, no separate ObjectCodegen pass)
        else cache miss (no sidecar, version mismatch, or source changed)
            Cache -->> PW: CacheLookupResult::Miss
            Note over PW, ST_m1: Phase 0 already ran in register_module — structural decls are present.<br/>Defn authorship ordering is per-entry (ModuleEntry::Def.seq allocated at form-loop insert via SymbolTable::next_seq.fetch_add(1)).<br/>Worker proceeds directly to the form loop with [&SymbolTable] via Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(m1).

            loop one cluster (file's non-structural forms in source order, from saved cursor on resume)
                Note over PW, Sched: process_cluster is the orchestrator. Signature — shared ref to SharedState, forms as Vec of Sexp, scope as ref to m1. Per Decision 44 amended by FIXME 0167 — 2026-05-13 third amendment.
                Note over PW, Sched: Frontend stays pure — no live mutation. Typecheck stays pure with respect to live state — mutates orchestrator-handed staging via ctx.current_symbol_table_mut.
                Note over PW, Sched: Neither has a Sess or scheduler dependency — they SURFACE dependencies as Err of CheckError.Gap of ResolutionGap. Per S76 W-Macro typecheck surfaces the MacroInMem gap on recognising a not-yet-jitted macro, and the retired frontend ExpansionError path is gone.
                Note over PW, Sched: process_cluster catches each gap and dispatches via handle_gap — ensure_registered then wait then priority_boost plus wait_for_inmem — and RETRIES the call.
                Note over PW, Sched: Workers park inside scheduler wait_* — never inside library code. See facades/int.md section "process_cluster — the cluster-atomic orchestration loop".
                Note over PW, Sched: THREE-PASS model (S76 W-Macro DECISION LOCKED 2026-06-03 — macro-availability-model.md section 0 — resolution-primitive fold-in section 0.9). PASS 1 expand — int's process_cluster loop recognises macro heads via the cranelisp-types primitive resolve_macro_head over the committed view (zero int to typecheck dep for recognition), executes via the injected MacroExpander, build_forms the result, re-enters to fixpoint. Dependency-module forms a clause needs are typechecked-and-compiled just-in-time. Same-module non-macro defs are NOT available at expansion. PASS 2 plus PASS 3 — one check_forms call over the fully-expanded vec of ParsedEntry, internally registering non-macro signatures then checking non-macro bodies. Then cluster-atomic drain into live via insert_cluster.

                PW ->> Shared: Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(&m1)<br/>(shared shard read lock — concurrent with other workers' shared reads)
                Shared -->> PW: Some(Ref[SymbolTable]) ≡ [&SymbolTable]

                Note over PW, Sched: PASS 1 — EXPAND (S76 W-Macro DECISION LOCKED — resolution-primitive fold-in section 0.9). Macro expansion is NO LONGER a frontend.expand call. macro-availability-model.md section 0 + macro-expansion-ownership.md.<br/>int's process_cluster expand loop OWNS Pass 1: it recognises macro heads via the cranelisp-types primitive resolve_macro_head over the committed symbol tables (walk + macro-vs-fn discrimination via the types query, zero int to typecheck dep for recognition), executes via the injected MacroExpander, build_forms the result, and re-enters to fixpoint.<br/>defmacro-before-use is normative. A macro's expansion may reference DEPENDENCY-module defs (typechecked-before, fetched just-in-time) plus same-module MACROS — never same-module non-macro defs (those are Pass 2/3 entities, structurally invisible). Frontend does only quasiquote desugaring now.

                loop Pass 1 expand-loop to fixpoint — int drives, typecheck recognises, MacroExpander executes
                    opt macro head recognised whose clause code (or a dependency form it needs) is not yet in memory
                        Note over PW, Sched: int surfaces the just-in-time dependency need as a gap. handle_gap dispatch:
                        PW ->> Shared: ensure_registered(shared, &dep.module) — calls register_module_internal if absent (Phase 0 runs synchronously). Acyclic dependency graph — dep cannot refer back to m1.
                        Shared -->> PW: Ok(())
                        PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_for_typecheck_symbol(fq: &FQSymbol) -> Result[(), SchedulerError]
                        Note over PW, Sched: PW releases m1 and parks. Resumes when dep/sym typecheck-done (may be different priority worker on resume).
                        Sched -->> PW: Ok(())
                        Note over PW: peek at the now-typechecked entry — force code in-mem only when needed to EXECUTE a macro clause or its dependency:
                        opt entry needs JIT to be invoked at expansion (macro clause or its just-in-time dependency)
                            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::priority_boost_jit(fq: &FQSymbol)
                            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_for_inmem(fq: &FQSymbol) -> Result[(), SchedulerError]
                            Note over PW, Sched: PW parks. Sched promotes Jit(dep/sym) to head of priority queue.<br/>Some worker JITs dep/sym — on completion Sched releases the wait.<br/>NOTE — block_for_macro_codegen is DELETED, not wired — the locked decision forbids same-module non-macro clause callees, so there is no empty-slot case.
                            Sched -->> PW: Ok(()) — dep/sym jitted
                        end
                    end

                    opt macro head recognised with clause code in memory — EXECUTE via the injected MacroExpander
                        create participant Expander as MacroExpander impl<br/>cranelisp_types::MacroExpander (int-owned)<br/>src::expander invocation core + src::marshal
                        PW ->> Expander: MacroExpander::invoke(fq: &FQSymbol, args: &[Sexp], call_span: Span) -> Result[Sexp, MacroInvokeError]
                        Note over PW, Expander: int marshals args to runtime ADT (src::marshal), transmutes the GOT'd clause to extern "C" fn(i64)->i64, calls it under sigsetjmp/siglongjmp signal protection, unmarshals + rewrites spans (fresh synthetic spans).
                        Expander -->> PW: Ok(Sexp) — expanded result. int build_forms it and re-enters the loop — nested-macro fixpoint plus structural-form re-entry (def to begin-defn-defmacro) per macro-availability-model.md section 0.7.
                    end
                end

                opt introspection enabled (REPL or trace mode)
                    Note over PW, Shared: populate per-defn metadata at parse-time per Decision 38 + 39
                    PW ->> Shared: Sess.shared.introspection.as_ref().map(|m| m.insert(fq, Introspection { source: ... slice from file Arc[str] ..., sexp: Some(expanded.clone()), ..Default::default() }))
                end

                PW ->> Frontend: cranelisp_frontend::build_form — defn_sexp as &Sexp returns Result of vec of ParsedEntry or CranelispError
                Note over PW, Frontend: S66 FIXME 0156 — returns vec of ParsedEntry because some shapes yield more than one entry per source form.
                Note over PW, Frontend: Multi-clause defmacro emits one parent Def of kind Macro — metadata only — plus one Def of kind UserFn per clause body under mangled name {macro}$clause-{N} per cranelisp_types::DefKind::Macro.
                Note over PW, Frontend: deftype emits the type Def plus one Constructor-kind Def per ctor per D49.
                Note over PW, Frontend: For trailing-expression forms the REPL path calls build_expr instead — sexp as &Sexp returns Result of Expr or CranelispError — chosen at the call site, no AST union enum.
                Frontend -->> PW: Ok of vec of ParsedEntry — untyped. build_form and build_expr have no gaps — pure transform.

                alt form is import [m2 ...] — peeled off by extract_module_declarations BEFORE build_form, not gap-driven
                    Note over PW, Sched: import is structurally classified BEFORE build_form (extract_module_declarations) — process_form invokes scheduler explicitly to wait for m2 and update local bindings.
                    PW ->> Shared: ensure_registered(shared, &m2.module)
                    Shared -->> PW: Ok(())
                    PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_for_typecheck(module: &ModuleFullPath) -> Result[(), SchedulerError]
                    Note over PW, Sched: PW releases m1 and parks until m2 typecheck-done<br/>(import must update local symbol table with FQ → bare bindings)
                    Sched -->> PW: Ok(())
                    PW ->> Shared: Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(&m2)
                    Shared -->> PW: Some(Ref[SymbolTable])
                    create participant ST_m2 as ST[m2]<br/>SymbolTable [generic C=Code, L=()]
                    PW ->> ST_m2: SymbolTable::public_symbols() -> Iterator[(&Symbol, &ModuleEntry[Code])]
                    ST_m2 -->> PW: iterator over (&Symbol, &ModuleEntry[Code]) for each export
                    PW ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::install_import_bindings(from: &ModuleFullPath, names: ImportNames)<br/>([&self] — writes Import-variant entries via inner DashMap per-key locks)
                else FQ form — the catch-all — defns, defmacros, deftypes, deftraits, impls, top-level exprs
                    create participant Typecheck as Typecheck facade<br/>cranelisp_typecheck
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: After PASS 1 expand has run to fixpoint (int's expand loop above) and build_form has accumulated the fully-expanded vec of ParsedEntry for the cluster, the orchestrator makes one cranelisp_typecheck::check_forms call for PASSES 2 plus 3.
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: Multi-clause defmacro yields one parent Macro-kind Def plus N clause-body UserFn Defs under {macro}$clause-{N} names. deftype-with-constructors yields the type Def plus N Constructor-kind Defs. Both shapes produce multiple ParsedEntry items per source form.
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: Per Decision 44 — amended by FIXME 0167 for Approach B plus SymbolTableAccess, and 2026-05-13 third amendment collapsing the two-pass split — check_forms internally registers non-macro signatures (Pass 2) then checks non-macro bodies (Pass 3) across all parsed entries. Macro expansion (Pass 1) already completed before this call, so check_forms never triggers macro execution and Decision 44 atomic-commit is intact over the expanded set.
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: The orchestrator constructs SymbolTableAccess.Cluster carrying modules, staging as mutable ref to empty_staging, and current_module once per cluster, then threads &mut ctx through the single check_forms call.
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: Typecheck mutates staging via ctx.current_symbol_table_mut — cluster-atomic drain at the end. The Pass-2-to-Pass-3 working state lives inside check_forms frame and never crosses the facade.

                    PW ->> Typecheck: cranelisp_typecheck::check_forms — parsed as vec of ParsedEntry, ctx as &mut SymbolTableAccess over Code and unit, symbol_tables as &SymbolTables, returns Result of unit or CheckError
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: Decision 44 third amendment — pure with respect to live state. Staging mutation flows through ctx.current_symbol_table_mut — same accessor used in committed-mode. The 91 register-call sites in typecheck program.rs do NOT change individually.
                    Note over PW, Typecheck: Pass 2 bodies check against ctx.current_symbol_table which returns a union View over staging and live in Cluster mode — cluster signatures from Pass 1 visible to Pass 2 internally.

                    opt check_forms returns gap — FQ value or fn ref m2/foo needs typecheck. Code not needed since macros are already expanded.
                        Typecheck -->> PW: Err of CheckError.Gap of ResolutionGap.SymbolTypechecked carrying m2/foo
                        Note over PW, Sched: process_cluster handle_gap dispatch on SymbolTypechecked. Per FIXME 0160 plus Decision 44 third amendment — live table is unchanged. Orchestrator drops the staging frame and retries the whole check_forms call against a fresh staging frame.
                        PW ->> Shared: ensure_registered — shared and ref to m2/foo.module
                        Shared -->> PW: Ok of unit
                        PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_for_typecheck_symbol — fq as &FQSymbol returns Result of unit or SchedulerError
                        Note over PW, Sched: PW releases m1 and parks. Typecheck waits do NOT priority-boost — m2 typecheck progresses naturally.
                        Sched -->> PW: Ok of unit
                        PW ->> Typecheck: cranelisp_typecheck::check_forms retried — parsed, &mut ctx, etc — with fresh staging
                    end

                    opt check_forms returns gap — FQ type ref m2/SomeType needs typecheck
                        Typecheck -->> PW: Err of CheckError.Gap of ResolutionGap.Type carrying m2/SomeType
                        Note over PW, Sched: process_cluster handle_gap dispatch on Type.
                        PW ->> Shared: ensure_registered — shared and ref to m2/SomeType.module
                        Shared -->> PW: Ok of unit
                        PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_for_typecheck_type — fqt as &FQTypeName returns Result of unit or SchedulerError
                        Sched -->> PW: Ok of unit
                        PW ->> Typecheck: cranelisp_typecheck::check_forms retried — parsed, &mut ctx, etc — with fresh staging
                    end

                    Typecheck -->> PW: Ok of unit — cluster fully checked. Staging carries body-checked entries with per-symbol Pass-2 side products on staging Def fields.

                    Note over PW, ST_m1: After check_forms returns Ok, the orchestrator drops ctx — releases the &mut staging borrow — and int::insert_cluster commits staging into the live SymbolTable atomically. Per-entry inner DashMap writes — no whole-module lock.
                    Note over PW, ST_m1: Order matters for ADT — type Def then Constructor-kind Defs per D49 — and multi-clause defmacro — parent Macro-kind metadata Def then each clause-body UserFn Def under {macro}$clause-{N} per cranelisp_types::DefKind::Macro. Order is preserved by build_form emission order, threaded through staging.
                    loop for each (sym, entry) in drained staging
                        PW ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::insert_or_update — sym as Symbol, entry as ModuleEntry over Code
                        Note over PW, ST_m1: Takes &self — inner DashMap per-entry write lock briefly. Decision 41 carry-forward of existing code field. Formerly Decision 31, retired.
                    end
                end

                PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_symbol_typechecked(fq: &FQSymbol)
                opt symbol needs JIT codegen
                    PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::enqueue_jit(fq: FQSymbol)
                end
            end

            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_typecheck_done(module: &ModuleFullPath)
            Note over Sched: fresh-typecheck notification —<br/>per-symbol Jit items were already enqueued during the loop.<br/>After all in-mem code is ready, Sched enqueues NiceWork::ObjectCodegen(m1).
        end
    end

    rect rgb(220, 255, 220)
        Note over Sched, Cache: JIT CODEGEN PHASE — work item type determined by typecheck-phase cache outcome<br/>PriorityWork::LoadObject(m1) on cache-hit path (single batch) — PriorityWork::Jit(FQSymbol) on cache-miss path (per symbol)<br/>workers acquire shared Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(m1) — concurrent codegen of different symbols allowed (per-entry write locks via inner DashMap)

        alt PriorityWork::LoadObject(m1) — cache-hit path
            Sched -->> PW: Some(PriorityWork::LoadObject(m1: ModuleFullPath))
            PW ->> Cache: ObjectCache::load_object(module: &ModuleFullPath) -> Result[Vec[u8], CacheError]
            Cache -->> PW: Ok(Vec[u8]) — .o bytes
            create participant Backend as Backend facade<br/>cranelisp_backend
            PW ->> Backend: cranelisp_backend::load_object(module: &ModuleFullPath, object: &[u8], symbol_tables: &SymbolTables) -> Result[LinkerArtefact, CranelispError]
            Note over Backend, ST_m1: linker resolves each defined symbol of m1 by bare name (per Decision 36)
            Backend ->> ST_m1: got().store_slot(entry.got_slot, ptr) — for each defined symbol — backend writes the GOT slot (D41 #2)<br/>S66 post-rollback — call address lives in the GOT (single source of truth)
            opt GotObserver registered (per defined symbol — relaxed-load null check)
                Note over Backend, GotObs: extension-point emit at the load_object slot-population site — cranelisp_backend::got_observer rustdoc + bounded-contexts.md §3
                Backend ->> GotObs: GotObserver(GotEventTag::LinkerWrite, &GotEvent { module: m1, symbol, slot, ptr, provenance: GotProvenance::Linker { linker_addr } })
            end
            Backend -->> PW: Ok(LinkerArtefact { linker: Arc[Linker], ptrs: HashMap[Symbol, *const u8] })
            Note over PW, ST_m1: CALLER composes Code (D41 #1, S75 W2 Finding-A) — for each (symbol, ptr) in ptrs, int stores Code::Linker(linker.clone()) on ST_m1[symbol] via SymbolTable::write_code. Backend never constructs Code.
            PW ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::write_code(sym, Code::Linker(Arc[Linker])) — for each defined symbol (caller-side compose)
            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_inmem_codegen_batch_complete(module: &ModuleFullPath)
            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_object_codegen_complete(module: &ModuleFullPath)
            Note over Sched: cache-hit completes BOTH in-mem and object phases for m1 — object phase skipped
        else PriorityWork::Jit(FQSymbol) — cache-miss path — per Decision 41 per-symbol JIT cardinality (one compile_to_module call per symbol, fresh JITModule per call for per-redefinition reclaim)
            Sched -->> PW: Some(PriorityWork::Jit(fq: FQSymbol))
            PW ->> Shared: Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(&m1)
            Shared -->> PW: Some(Ref[SymbolTable])
            Note over PW, Backend: per-symbol JIT call site (Decision 41) — names is single-element [fq.symbol].<br/>int creates the Jit, passes jit.jit_module() (a &mut M) into the call. Backend writes ONLY the GOT slot (D41 #2) and returns a value CompilationArtifacts (S70 Phase B amendment).<br/>Backend does NOT construct Code and does NOT name Introspection (S75 W2 Finding-A — backend only borrows &mut M, never owns the Arc[Jit]).
            PW ->> Backend: cranelisp_backend::compile_to_module[M: Module](scope: &ModuleFullPath, names: &[Symbol], symbol_tables: &SymbolTables[Code, ()], module_aliases: &ModuleAliases, module: jit.jit_module(), capture_clif: bool) -> Result[CompilationArtifacts, CompilationError]
            Backend ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::get(sym: &Symbol) -> Option[Ref[ModuleEntry[Code]]] — read ast, scheme, resolved calls
            Backend ->> ST_m1: got().store_slot(entry.got_slot, ptr)<br/>S66 post-rollback — call address lives in the GOT (single source of truth) — [&self] + inner DashMap per-key write lock, atomic GOT slot swap per Decision 41 (formerly Decision 31, retired)
            opt GotObserver registered (relaxed-load null check)
                Note over Backend, GotObs: extension-point emit at the got().store_slot site — cranelisp_backend::got_observer rustdoc + bounded-contexts.md §3
                Backend ->> GotObs: GotObserver(GotEventTag::JitWrite, &GotEvent { module: m1, symbol, slot, ptr, provenance: GotProvenance::Jit { jit_addr } })
            end
            Backend -->> PW: Ok(CompilationArtifacts { clif_ir, code_size, compile_duration })
            Note over PW, ST_m1: CALLER composes Code + Introspection (D41 #1, S75 W2 Finding-A). int wraps Arc::new(jit) AFTER the call and stores Code::Jit(Arc[Jit]) on ST_m1[fq.symbol] via SymbolTable::write_code (atomic GOT-swap-precedes-old-Arc-drop discipline per D41).
            PW ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::write_code(fq.symbol, Code::Jit(Arc[Jit])) — caller-side compose
            opt REPL or trace mode (caller retains the artefact)
                Note over PW, Shared: int composes Introspection from CompilationArtifacts + parse/expansion fields. disasm via on-demand produce_disasm(fq, code_size, symbol_tables) when /disasm fires (S75 W2 Finding-C — caller-supplied code_size + capstone).
                PW ->> Shared: introspection.insert(fq, Introspection { clif_ir: Some(...), code_size: Some(...), compile_duration: Some(...), .. })
            end
            PW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_inmem_codegen_complete(fq: &FQSymbol)
            Note over Sched: when all m1/sym in-mem complete: Sched enqueues NiceWork::ObjectCodegen(m1)
        end
    end

    Note over Sched: when global in-mem complete fires (no pending in-mem work):
    Sched -->> Sess: in-mem complete signal (releases wait_inmem_complete park)
    Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(()) — wait_for_inmem_codegen returns

    Note over Initiator: Initiator may now eval / call any function. To wait on object codegen pre-exit:

    Initiator ->> Sess: CompilerSession::wait_for_object_codegen() -> Result<(), CranelispError> †
    Sess ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::wait_object_complete() -> Result<(), SchedulerError>
    Note over Initiator, Sched: blocked until object complete signal fires

    rect rgb(255, 245, 220)
        Note over Sched, Cache: OBJECT CODEGEN PHASE — only runs for cache-miss modules<br/>nice workers run in parallel across modules — never per-symbol within a module

        create participant NW as Nice Worker<br/>::worker::nice_worker_loop(Arc[SharedState])
        Sched -->> NW: Some(NiceWork::ObjectCodegen(m1: ModuleFullPath))<br/>(returned from take_object_codegen() the worker was parked in)
        NW ->> Shared: Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(&m1)
        Shared -->> NW: Some(Ref[SymbolTable])
        Note over NW, Backend: single codegen entry (Decision 23, design/backend/compile-to-module.md §2) — object mode is just an ObjectModule instance passed to the SAME compile_to_module[M].<br/>NO separate compile_to_object backend entry. The nice worker constructs the ObjectModule, calls compile_to_module::[ObjectModule], then FINALISES it caller-side (the §2.5 caller-finalize contract, symmetric to int holding the JITModule for Arc[Jit] reclaim in JIT mode).
        NW ->> NW: let mut obj_module = ObjectModule::new(ObjectBuilder::new(build_isa(true), ..))
        NW ->> Backend: cranelisp_backend::compile_to_module[M: Module](scope: &ModuleFullPath, names: &[Symbol], symbol_tables: &SymbolTables[Code, ()], module_aliases: &ModuleAliases, module: obj_module, capture_clif: bool) -> Result[CompilationArtifacts, CompilationError]
        Backend ->> ST_m1: SymbolTable::get(sym: &Symbol) — for each defined symbol of m1
        Backend -->> NW: Ok(CompilationArtifacts { clif_ir, code_size, compile_duration })
        NW ->> NW: let product = obj_module.finish() then let obj_bytes = product.emit()? — caller-side finalize (the §2.5 contract — backend never touches disk)
        Note over NW, Cache: nice worker packages obj_bytes + serialised SymbolTable[(), ()] sidecar into the ObjectArtefact it persists
        NW ->> Cache: ObjectCache::write(module: &ModuleFullPath, artefact: &ObjectArtefact { object: obj_bytes, sidecar }) -> Result[(), CacheError]
        NW ->> Sched: CompileScheduler::notify_object_codegen_complete(module: &ModuleFullPath)
    end

    Sched -->> Sess: object complete signal (releases wait_object_complete park)
    Sess -->> Initiator: Ok(()) — wait_for_object_codegen returns
